description_current:
Colleen Gillis of Cooley is requesting a zoning verification for 45449 E. Severn Way - PIN: 030-15-5049. 

1. That the Property is zoned to the PD-IP (Planned Development-Industrial Park) district per the Revised 1993 Loudoun County Zoning Ordinance (the "Zoning Ordinance"), which allows development at an intensity up to a 0.6 Floor Area Ratio by-right pursuant to Section 4-506 of the Zoning Ordinance or at an intensity up to a 1.0 Floor Area Ratio by Special Exception as approved by the Loudoun County Board of Supervisors, pursuant to Section 6-1300 of the Zoning Ordinance;
2 . That the Property is subject to ZRTD-2021 -0009, approved June 21, 2022, and the proffers and concept development plan approved with that application and that there are no other legislative approvals that pertain to the Property;
3. That pursuant to Sections 4-503 and 4-506 of the Zoning Ordinance, a data center use at an intensity up to a 0.6 Floor Area Ratio may be developed by-right on the Property;
4 . That there are no known or pending zoning violations pertaining to the Property; and
5. That (i) all approvals and other permits issued to date by the County were issued in accordance with all applicable state laws, County ordinances and regulations and (ii) there are no proceedings pertaining to the Property, either administrative or legislative, which would in any manner adversely affect the status of the zoning of the Property.

Erin Swisshelm of Walsh Colucci is requesting a zoning verification request for Loudoun County PIN: 089-49-6246.
1. That the Property is zoned to the PD-OP (Planned Development - Office Park) zoning district pursuant to the Revised 1993 Loudoun County Zoning Ordinance;
2. That data centers are a permitted use on the Property;
3. That the Property is subject to Worldcom/ULJNet ZMAP-1998-0003, including a
Proffer Statement dated June 17, 1998 (the "Worldcom Proffers");
4. That the Property may be developed with a density of 0.4 FAR by right, and up to 0.6 FAR by Special Exception;
5. That there are no known or pending zoning or proffer violations pertaining to the
Property; and
6. That (i) all approvals and other permits issued to date by the County were issued in
accordance with all applicable state laws, County ordinances and regulations and (ii)
there are no proceedings pertaining to the Property, either administrative or legislative, which would in any manner adversely affect the status of the zoning of the Property.
